## 1. Starting canonical endpoint

The Target B sufficient closure is

\[
G+E\ge c_0B+a_0(t+\chi-1),\qquad
a_0=\sqrt3/2,\quad c_0=\sqrt3/4.
\]

For a pure rhombic disk, \(t=0\) and \(\chi=1\), while the promoted global
minimizer comparison gives the strict reverse inequality \(G+E<c_0B\). The
open endpoint is still the global coupling of grain and interface terms, or an
actual same-cardinality strict smaller-diameter competitor. The result below
does not prove that closure.

The original affine-source chain was

```text
one bounded-displacement oblique-lattice chart
  -> sublinear convex-hull lattice boundary count
  -> exact Pick ledger for a pure rhombic disk
  -> restricted near-triangular shear and shell-gap information
```

It ends with a narrow survivor, not a contradiction. I then pursued a separate
global disproof chain:

```text
one actual global minimizer with a single diameter direction
  -> a source-preserving affine stretch with the same diameter
  -> a triangle-free global minimizer of the same cardinality
```

The second chain is proved conditionally. The missing part is an unbounded
sequence of global minimizers with that diameter-graph property.

## 2. Strongest new result: affine flat modes create tied minimizers

### General affine criterion

Let \(A\subset\mathbb R^2\) be a finite unit-separated set with diameter
\(D>0\). Let \(\mathcal C\) be the difference vectors of unit-distance
pairs and \(\mathcal M\) the difference vectors of diametral pairs. Suppose
there is a nonzero symmetric matrix \(Q\) such that

\[
c^{\mathsf T}Qc\ge0\quad(c\in\mathcal C),\qquad
m^{\mathsf T}Qm\le0\quad(m\in\mathcal M),
\tag{6}
\]

at least one \(m_0\in\mathcal M\) has \(m_0^{\mathsf T}Qm_0=0\), and every
unit equilateral triangle in \(A\) has at least one side vector \(c\) with
\(c^{\mathsf T}Qc>0\). Then an invertible affine image of \(A\) is
unit-separated, has the same diameter and cardinality, and contains no unit
equilateral triangle. If \(A\) is a global minimizer, the image is a
triangle-free global minimizer of the same cardinality.

### Proof

For \(t>0\) small, \(G_t=I+tQ\) is positive definite. Choose an invertible
linear map \(T_t\) with \(T_t^{\mathsf T}T_t=G_t\). For every pair difference
\(v\),

\[
|T_tv|^2=|v|^2+t\,v^{\mathsf T}Qv.
\tag{7}
\]

For unit pairs, (6) keeps the squared distance at least one. All other pair
distances initially lie strictly above one; finiteness lets us choose \(t\)
small enough that none drops to one. For diametral pairs, (6) keeps every
squared distance at most \(D^2\), and \(m_0\) remains at \(D\). Every
non-diametral pair initially has squared distance strictly below \(D^2\);
again, finiteness lets us choose \(t\) small enough that none reaches \(D\).
So \(T_t(A)\) is unit-separated and has diameter exactly \(D\).

Any unit triangle in the image must come from three source pairs of unit
length: noncontacts remain strictly above one, and contacts do not contract.
Those three source sides already form a unit equilateral triangle. By
hypothesis at least one side has \(c^{\mathsf T}Qc>0\), so (7) makes its image
length strictly greater than one. This rules out every unit triangle in the
image.

If \(A\) is globally minimizing, it has diameter \(D(n)\). The constructed
feasible set has the same cardinality and diameter \(D(n)\), so it is also a
global minimizer. \(\square\)

### One-direction stretch corollary

Suppose all diametral difference vectors are parallel to a fixed line with
unit direction \(e\). Let \(f\perp e\) be unit and set \(Q=ff^{\mathsf T}\).
Then \(v^{\mathsf T}Qv=(v\cdot f)^2\ge0\) for every pair, while every
diametral vector has value zero. A unit equilateral triangle cannot have all
three sides parallel to \(e\), so every triangle has a side on which \(Q>0\).
The general criterion applies. In this case the exact map is
\(T_s=I+sff^{\mathsf T}\), whose squared-length change is
\((2s+s^2)(v\cdot f)^2\).

Thus **any** global minimizer with only one diametral direction has a
triangle-free global-minimizer tie at the same \(n\). An unbounded sequence
of such minimizers would disprove Level I.

### A checkable sector condition

The affine criterion also handles several diameter directions. Suppose \(A\)
contains a unit triangle whose side-direction lines include consecutive lines
at angles \(\alpha\) and \(\beta=\alpha+\pi/3\). Assume:

1. no unit-distance pair has direction strictly inside the open sector
   \((\alpha,\beta)\), modulo \(\pi\);
2. every diametral pair has direction in the closed sector
   \([\alpha,\beta]\), modulo \(\pi\).

Let \(a,b\) be unit vectors on the boundary lines and define
\[
v^{\mathsf T}Qv=(v\cdot a^\perp)(v\cdot b^\perp).
\]
This quadratic form is negative inside the sector, zero on its boundary, and
positive outside. Thus all unit contacts have nonnegative \(Q\), all
diametral pairs have nonpositive \(Q\), and at least one side direction of
every unit triangle has positive \(Q\): a triangle has three distinct side
lines, while only two lines are zeros and none lies in the open sector.

If a global minimizer satisfied these conditions with every diametral pair
strictly inside the sector, (7) would strictly reduce its diameter, a
contradiction. Therefore a global minimizer satisfying the two conditions
must have a diametral pair on the sector boundary. That pair stays at \(D\),
so the affine criterion gives a triangle-free global minimizer of the same
cardinality. This is a finite, source-level test for another disproof route;
it does not assert that any global minimizer meets the sector conditions.

### Scope and limit

These are exact finite-set theorems in the original plane. They use the actual
source points and all unit and diametral pairs. They do not assume a lattice,
jammedness, or a shell model. They are not a Level I disproof: no unbounded
family meeting either sufficient condition has been constructed or proved to
exist.

## 3. Independent audit of the affine-lattice candidate

The audited candidate is
`docs/reports/target_b_affine_boundary_shear_2026-09-25.md` at source commit
`eec3f364f2e2e4ed1b85be44234d036b893cdb31`; the exact source file hash is
