## 8. Handoff

1. **Strongest new theorem:** any nonzero affine flat mode satisfying (6),
   with one fixed diameter pair and strict expansion on at least one side of
   every source triangle, produces a triangle-free same-diameter configuration.
2. **Dependencies:** none beyond finite-set geometry; for the independent
   affine audit, Target B Sections 36, 38.1, and 48.1.
3. **Exact remaining lemma:** establish an unbounded family of global
   minimizers whose actual contact-diameter data admit a matrix \(Q\) with
   the signs in (6), or prove that every sufficiently large global minimizer
   lacks every such affine flat mode. The one-direction and sector conditions
   above are explicit sufficient cases.
4. **Binding dead routes:** Pick-only shell contradiction; scalar strict
   diameter bound as a global-optimality certificate; treating an affine
   source chart as supplied by the general almost-rhombic branch.
5. **Next files:** `docs/targets/target-b/README.md`, Target B Sections
   36--48, and the exact source candidate at the commit/hash stated above.
